===Etymology===
Probably the diminutive of {{etyl|es}} {{term|macho|lang=es||sledgehammer}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|masculus|lang=la}}, diminutive of classical {{term|mas|mās|lang=la}}, ultimately from {{proto|Indo-European|meh₂s}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sword]]-like [[tool]] used for [[cut]]ting large [[plant]]s with a [[chop]]ping motion. A machete's blade is usually 50 to 65 centimeters ([[cm]]) long, and up to three millimeters ([[mm]]) thick.

